258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (ABOUT THE HIDDEN HORRORS)
/E (ABOUT THE HIDDEN HORRORS)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The lifetime impact of Child Sexual Abuse Material \(CSAM\) on children is profound and multifaceted, affecting various aspects of their well-being. Key impacts include:)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 770 0 R
/ActualText (Psychological Trauma: Victims often experience long-term psychological effects such as depression, anxiety, PTSD, and suicidal ideation. The trauma of the abuse itself, compounded by knowing the material is circulating online, exacerbates these conditions.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 771 0 R
/ActualText (Social and Emotional Consequences: Children may struggle with trust issues, forming healthy relationships, and social isolation. The stigma and shame associated with the abuse can lead to a sense of hopelessness and low self-esteem.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 772 0 R
/ActualText (Cognitive and Academic Difficulties: The stress and trauma can hinder cognitive development and academic performance. Children may exhibit difficulties in concentrating, learning, and maintaining academic progress.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 773 0 R
/ActualText (Physical Health Issues: The stress and anxiety can manifest in physical health problems, including sleep disorders, eating disorders, and other stress-related illnesses.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 774 0 R
/ActualText (Risk of Re-victimization: Victims of CSAM are at higher risk of being re-victimized both online and offline. The persistent presence of their abuse material online can lead to ongoing exploitation and harassment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 775 0 R
/ActualText (Challenges in Recovery and Support: Accessing appropriate mental health care and support services can be difficult, and the process of recovery is often long and complex. The need for specialized care is crucial for the healing process.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 191 0 R
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (INTRODUCTION)
/E (INTRODUCTION)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (CSAM perpetuates a cycle of victimization for children by stripping them of their personal safety and right to privacy, while inflicting great and lasting harm. Reducing the availability of this material must be a key pillar of child protection frameworks in our efforts to keep citizens safe.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The criminal nature of much of the material itself presents barriers from a research, public awareness and policy development perspective. Over time, these barriers have resulted in a limited understanding of the nature of the material, how it flourishes online and the manner in which it is distributed or accessed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (THE DANGERS OF CSAM AND CHILD EXPLOITATION)
/E (THE DANGERS OF CSAM AND CHILD EXPLOITATION)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (About 98% of reported CSAM involved children under the age of 13, with 30% under 10, including infants and toddlers.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
