<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 192 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Definition of CSAM)
/E (Definition of CSAM)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Child Sexual Abusive Material \(CSAM\) refers to any visual depiction of sexually explicit conduct involving a minor \(someone under 18 years of age\). This includes photographs, videos, and digital images, as well as other media formats. The term encompasses a broad range of content that can include:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 776 0 R
/ActualText (Explicit Sexual Activity: Images or videos showing minors engaged in sexual acts, whether with adults, other minors, or alone.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 777 0 R
/ActualText (Sexualized Posing: Any content where minors are posed in sexually suggestive ways, even if no explicit sexual activity is shown.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 778 0 R
/ActualText (Digitally Created Content: Computer-generated or altered images that depict minors in sexually explicit scenarios.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 779 0 R
/ActualText (Real and Simulated Content: Both real images/videos of minors and those created or altered to appear as such, including deepfakes.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 780 0 R
/ActualText (Self-Generated Content: Images or videos created by the minors themselves, often under coercion or exploitation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (CSAM is illegal and is recognized globally as a serious form of child exploitation and abuse. Efforts to combat CSAM include stringent laws, international cooperation, technology for detection and prevention, and extensive support services for victims.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Importance of addressing CSAM)
/E (Importance of addressing CSAM)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Addressing Child Sexual Abuse Material \(CSAM\) is crucial due to its profound and lasting impact on victims, the pervasive nature of its distribution, and the broader societal implications. Tackling this issue involves protecting vulnerable children, preventing future abuses, and holding perpetrators accountable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (PREVALENCE OF CSAM)
/E (PREVALENCE OF CSAM)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/T (The prevalence of Child Sexual Abusive Material \(CSAM\) is a pressing global issue, reflecting the widespread and growing nature of child exploitation and abuse. While precise figures are difficult to ascertain due to the clandestine nature of these activities, various studies, reports, and statistics shed light on the scope of the problem.)
/E (The prevalence of Child Sexual Abusive Material \(CSAM\) is a pressing global issue, reflecting the widespread and growing nature of child exploitation and abuse. While precise figures are difficult to ascertain due to the clandestine nature of these activities, various studies, reports, and statistics shed light on the scope of the problem.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 781 0 R
/ActualText (Internet and Dark Web: The internet, especially the dark web, has significantly increased the accessibility and distribution of CSAM. Offenders use encrypted communication and anonymous browsing to share and trade abusive material.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 782 0 R
/ActualText (Social Media Platforms: Social media and instant messaging apps have become channels for the rapid dissemination of CSAM, often through covert groups and networks.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Global statistics of CSAM)
/E (Global statistics of CSAM)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 783 0 R
/ActualText (In 2022, 64.5% of reported CSAM websites were in Asia, 5.2% in Europe, 8.3% in North America, and 10% in Africa.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 784 0 R
